WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.857 --> 00:00:12.198
go fishing," Dad said one day.

2
00:00:12.218 --> 00:00:14.780
"I'll teach you how to fish."

3
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.581
"Yes!" I cried.

4
00:00:20.423 --> 00:00:21.904
Dad and I drove to a shop.

5
00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.768
We bought hooks, floats, and worms for bait.

6
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.242
We also bought fishing line for our rods.

7
00:00:34.543 --> 00:00:35.924
Then we headed to the river.

8
00:00:37.065 --> 00:00:39.486
Dad pointed to a small motorboat at a dock.

9
00:00:40.587 --> 00:00:41.948
"That's our boat!"

10
00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:46.011
The boat rocked as we climbed in.

11
00:00:48.812 --> 00:00:49.933
Dad started the motor.

12
00:00:50.273 --> 00:00:55.497
Vroom! Finally we stopped in the middle of the river.

13
00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:58.859
"Time to fish!"

14
00:00:59.319 --> 00:00:59.860
Dad said.

15
00:01:01.684 --> 00:01:04.306
He helped me tie a hook and float to my fishing rod.

16
00:01:07.148 --> 00:01:08.549
Then I looked at the tub of bait.

17
00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:11.591
I picked out the biggest worm.

18
00:01:11.611 --> 00:01:14.653
"Dad, let's put this one on my hook.

19
00:01:17.174 --> 00:01:18.635
I'll catch a huge fish!"

20
00:01:20.797 --> 00:01:21.557
Dad smiled.

21
00:01:24.099 --> 00:01:24.759
"We'll see!"

22
00:01:26.481 --> 00:01:28.762
He showed me how to cast the line into the water.

23
00:01:33.472 --> 00:01:36.815
"Now we must wait for the fish to bite," he said.

24
00:01:39.497 --> 00:01:40.938
We waited and waited.

25
00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:46.263
But the fish did not bite!

26
00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:49.685
"Look!" Dad said suddenly.

27
00:01:50.866 --> 00:01:53.248
The float on my line was bobbing up and down!

28
00:01:56.571 --> 00:01:58.272
Dad helped me reel in the line.

29
00:01:59.613 --> 00:02:00.454
I grinned.

30
00:02:00.474 --> 00:02:02.316
"I caught a fish!

31
00:02:03.472 --> 00:02:05.173
Now I'm a real fisherman!"

32
00:02:05.193 --> 00:02:07.635
"Yes, you are!"

33
00:02:08.015 --> 00:02:08.596
Dad said.

34
00:02:08.616 --> 00:02:11.738
"But this fish is too small to keep.

35
00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:14.760
We have to toss it back."

36
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.422
"Ugh," I groaned.

37
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:22.045
We let the fish go, and it quickly swam away.

38
00:02:23.746 --> 00:02:25.527
Soon I cast out the line again.

39
00:02:26.588 --> 00:02:28.889
The air grew cold as we waited some more.

40
00:02:28.909 --> 00:02:33.728
"Dad, I'm cold," I said.

41
00:02:33.748 --> 00:02:36.310
"And bored."

42
00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:37.931
Dad nodded.

43
00:02:37.951 --> 00:02:41.733
"Fishermen do a lot of waiting!"

44
00:02:43.914 --> 00:02:46.175
Just then a big boat passed by.

45
00:02:50.377 --> 00:02:53.519
we can fish on a boat like that someday," Dad said.

46
00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:57.641
"We can fish on the ocean and catch all kinds of fish.

47
00:02:58.061 --> 00:02:59.182
Really big ones."

48
00:02:59.202 --> 00:03:02.944
"Thanks," I said.

49
00:03:04.588 --> 00:03:06.029
"But fishing is boring.

50
00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:08.471
I'm not sure—" "Look!"

51
00:03:08.952 --> 00:03:09.692
Dad cried.

52
00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:12.875
My line was bobbing again!

53
00:03:15.177 --> 00:03:17.338
This time I reeled it in by myself.

54
00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.923
caught a big, beautiful trout!"

55
00:03:23.283 --> 00:03:23.903
Dad said.

56
00:03:26.566 --> 00:03:27.767
I was so proud.

57
00:03:27.787 --> 00:03:31.570
"Dad, can we go fishing again tomorrow?"

58
00:03:32.751 --> 00:03:33.591
Dad laughed.

59
00:03:36.252 --> 00:03:37.815
"I thought you didn't like fishing!"

60
00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:39.619
I shook my head.

61
00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:41.903
"I love it!"
